cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TamaBench in your research, please cite it as follows."
title: "TamaBench: A Lightweight Persistent Sandbox Benchmark for Small Language Model Autonomy"
abstract: >-
  TamaBench is a lightweight long-horizon benchmark for small and local LLM
  agents and the automation harnesses that extend them. Agents operate a
  persistent sandbox (care, work, economy, delayed consequences) and are
  scored on survival, planning, tool reliability, resource management, and
  compute efficiency. The benchmark measures how much autonomy can be
  extracted from a small model before a larger model is needed, and how
  much an automation harness can close that gap.
